":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2023-6476","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-770","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-770"},{"subject":"CVE-2023-6476","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2023-6476","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"assigner","object":"GitHub_M","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"github_m"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"8.6","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"8.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"HIGH","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"high"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"date-published","object":"2024-01-31T21:31:14.391Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2024-01-31t21:31:14.391z"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-17T12:04:33.454Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-17t12:04:33.454z"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"description","object":"runc is a CLI tool for spawning and running containers on Linux according to the OCI specification. In runc 1.1.11 and earlier, due to an internal file descriptor leak, an attacker could cause a newly-spawned container process (from runc exec) to have a working directory in the host filesystem namespace, allowing for a container escape by giving access to the host filesystem (\"attack 2\"). The same attack could be used by a malicious image to allow a container process to gain access to the host filesystem through runc run (\"attack 1\"). Variants of attacks 1 and 2 could be also be used to overwrite semi-arbitrary host binaries, allowing for complete container escapes (\"attack 3a\" and \"attack 3b\"). runc 1.1.12 includes patches for this issue.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"runc is a cli tool for spawning and running containers on linux according to the oci specification. in runc 1.1.11 and earlier, due to an internal file descriptor leak, an attacker could cause a newly-spawned container process (from runc exec) to have a working directory in the host filesystem namespace, allowing for a container escape by giving access to the host filesystem (\"attack 2\"). the same attack could be used by a malicious image to allow a container process to gain access to the host filesystem through runc run (\"attack 1\"). variants of attacks 1 and 2 could be also be used to overwrite semi-arbitrary host binaries, allowing for complete container escapes (\"attack 3a\" and \"attack 3b\"). runc 1.1.12 includes patches for this issue."},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"product","object":"runc","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"runc"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-403","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-403"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-668","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-668"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-21626","predicate":"vendor","object":"opencontainers","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"opencontainers"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-5037","predicate":"affects-cpe","object":"cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4.12::el8","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4.12::el8"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-5037","predicate":"affects-cpe","obj